[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585608845","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-2585608845","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":2585608845,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aHUKN","user":{"login":"carsonetb","id":63245844,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjQ1ODQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63245844?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb","html_url":"https://github.com/carsonetb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-12T06:34:34Z","updated_at":"2025-01-12T06:34:34Z","body":"Ok, I just restarted the editor and now I can't reproduce the bug. After a little bit of finicking I realized the problem is a little bit weirder than that.\n\nIf you create a new `ParticleProcessMaterial` as the Process Material, you can select the dropdown and choose \"Convert to ShaderMaterial\". After that, if you change the `shader` property of the new resource to a custom shader via the quick load option, this bug occurs.\n\nNice.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585608845/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585621147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-2585621147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":2585621147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aHXKb","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-12T07:26:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-12T07:28:07Z","body":"Does the bug still happen if you use \n```\nuniform float gravity = 98.0; \n```\n\nInstead of \n```\nuniform float gravity = 98;\n```\n\nIt sounds like the problem comes from the code that interprets the default value for that uniform. You have a float uniform, but you are telling it to default to an int value. I suspect this leads to the actual value getting set to 0","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585621147/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585830155","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-2585830155","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":2585830155,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aIKML","user":{"login":"carsonetb","id":63245844,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjQ1ODQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63245844?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb","html_url":"https://github.com/carsonetb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-12T16:46:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-12T16:46:24Z","body":"Yes the bug still happens. I don't think the extra decimal matters for uniform floats. Even if you change the value in the editor this glitch still happens.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585830155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2600994179","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-2600994179","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":2600994179,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bCAWD","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-19T19:38:08Z","updated_at":"2025-01-19T20:25:49Z","body":"I did a test and actually seems the engine is trying to pass the values from current shader uniform to the new shader. If you use any uniform name that don't collide with the old shader uniforms, everything will works as expected.\n\nUsing the mrp, the `gravity` uniform will receive the value from the converted particle material `gravity`, but because is a `vec3` being assigned to a `float`, the assign will fail and the `gravity` uniform reset to the default float value, 0.0:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b60484b0-3ce4-485e-901b-6b75cc0fa1e8\n\n<br>\n\nIf you set a value for the uniform in the inspector, the bug stops (needs to be a different value to trigger the `value_changed` signal):\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a810195-aae1-4ff8-b595-f77767a40b37\n\n<br>\n\nNow if we change the uniform name to `spread` you will notice the new shader will inherit the value from the old shader because both values are `float`\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/38f7f331-07e9-4e53-a12a-f0c446b29b39\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2600994179/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3085065090","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-3085065090","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":3085065090,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc634luC","user":{"login":"Fireye04","id":45439844,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NDM5ODQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45439844?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04","html_url":"https://github.com/Fireye04","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Fireye04/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-17T18:40:38Z","updated_at":"2025-07-17T18:40:38Z","body":"> If you create a new `ParticleProcessMaterial` as the Process Material, you can select the dropdown and choose \"Convert to ShaderMaterial\". After that, if you change the `shader` property of the new resource to a custom shader via the quick load option, this bug occurs.\n\nWow yeah, full repros arch/niri on 4.4.1 and 4.5beta3 using the above method. Crazy stuff!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3085065090/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3174575339","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-3174575339","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":3174575339,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69OCzr","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-11T12:34:24Z","updated_at":"2025-08-11T12:34:24Z","body":"Need to actually figure out why old uniforms are supplied and where in the chain of calls it happens. Ideas @clayjohn ?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3174575339/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3176122136","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-3176122136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":3176122136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc69T8cY","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-11T17:51:16Z","updated_at":"2025-08-11T17:51:16Z","body":"> Need to actually figure out why old uniforms are supplied and where in the chain of calls it happens. Ideas [@clayjohn](https://github.com/clayjohn) ?\n\nNot sure exactly, but the convert to shader button would be a good place to start https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ca452113d430cb96de409a297ff5b52389f1c9d9/editor/scene/material_editor_plugin.cpp#L548","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3176122136/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3240264658","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-3240264658","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":3240264658,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BIoPS","user":{"login":"carsonetb","id":63245844,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjQ1ODQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63245844?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb","html_url":"https://github.com/carsonetb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-31T16:40:36Z","updated_at":"2025-08-31T17:37:11Z","body":"I just did a little more testing, and it looks like the issue doesn't have anything to do with converting from a ParticleProcessMaterial. If you create a new ShaderMaterial with this script:\n\n```\nshader_type particles;\n\nuniform vec3 gravity;\n```\n\nAnd then change the script to the one I used before, you can still see this bug happening:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ab94f88b-a67f-4d49-9feb-15a3889c0ca1\n\nSo it seems the problem is that when the type of the variable is changed but the name stays the same, something breaks in the conversion logic. \n\nAnd also, the bug isn't even limited to particles at all, it happens with any shader:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ee647077-de7f-47e8-8fca-475e08fcd97a\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3240264658/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3240298974","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-3240298974","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":3240298974,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BIwne","user":{"login":"carsonetb","id":63245844,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjQ1ODQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63245844?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb","html_url":"https://github.com/carsonetb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-31T17:42:40Z","updated_at":"2025-08-31T17:42:40Z","body":"Okay, I've managed to fix the issue.\n\nWhen the shader is changed, the callback eventually runs this code if the type of the last variable is different than the type of the current variable:\n\n```\n// Property has never been edited or its type changed, retrieve with default value.\nVariant default_value = RenderingServer::get_singleton()->shader_get_parameter_default(shader->get_rid(), pi.name);\nparam_cache.insert(pi.name, default_value);\nremap_cache.insert(info.name, pi.name);\n```\n\nBut in the `set_shader_parameter` function (which updates the variable correctly when set) has this code:\n\n```\nVariant *v = param_cache.getptr(p_param);\nif (!v) {\n\t// Never assigned, also update the remap cache.\n\tremap_cache[\"shader_parameter/\" + p_param.operator String()] = p_param;\n\tparam_cache.insert(p_param, p_value);\n} else {\n\t*v = p_value;\n}\n\nif (p_value.get_type() == Variant::OBJECT) {\n\tRID tex_rid = p_value;\n\tif (tex_rid == RID()) {\n\t\tparam_cache.erase(p_param);\n\n\t\tif (material_rid.is_valid()) {\n\t\t\tRS::get_singleton()->material_set_param(material_rid, p_param, Variant());\n\t\t}\n\t} else if (material_rid.is_valid()) {\n\t\tRS::get_singleton()->material_set_param(material_rid, p_param, tex_rid);\n\t}\n} else if (material_rid.is_valid()) {\n\tRS::get_singleton()->material_set_param(material_rid, p_param, p_value);\n}\n```\n\nThe important part is the second to last line, `RS::get_singleton()->material_set_param(material_rid, p_param, p_value);`. I assume this is responsible for actually updating the value in the shader. This isn't called in the other function, leading to the bug we were seeing.\n\nIf we modify the code to be this:\n\n```\n// Property has never been edited or its type changed, retrieve with default value.\nVariant default_value = RenderingServer::get_singleton()->shader_get_parameter_default(shader->get_rid(), pi.name);\nparam_cache.insert(pi.name, default_value);\nremap_cache.insert(info.name, pi.name);\nRS::get_singleton()->material_set_param(_get_material(), pi.name, default_value);\n```\n\nThe bug goes away. Let me know if this is a feasible way to fix the bug or if it will cause side effects because I'm not very well versed in the codebase. Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3240298974/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4222651419","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101456#issuecomment-4222651419","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101456","id":4222651419,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc77sIwb","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-10T09:49:34Z","updated_at":"2026-04-10T09:49:34Z","body":"Reopening as #110287 is being reverted.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4222651419/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]